<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">Key engineering decisions</h2>
  <div class="space-y-4">
    <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#5a9100]">01</span>
      <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]"><strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Model constraints, not a calendar:</strong> Treating availability as a constraint-satisfaction problem is what lets Zennly handle multi-resource bookings a simple calendar can't.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#5a9100]">02</span>
      <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]"><strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Resolve conflicts, don't just flag them:</strong> Surfacing a double-booking isn't enough&mdash;Zennly proposes the fix and can apply it with approval.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
      <span class="mt-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] font-semibold text-[#5a9100]">03</span>
      <p class="text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280]"><strong class="font-semibold text-[#111827]">Reminders should adapt, not just fire on schedule:</strong> A reminder timed to when someone actually responds does more than one sent at a fixed hour.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="mb-12" data-reveal>
  <h2 class="mb-4 text-[26px] font-semibold leading-[1.2] tracking-tight text-[#111827] md:text-[30px]">About Zennly</h2>
  <p class="text-[16px] leading-relaxed text-[#6B7280] md:text-[17px]">
    Zennly is multi-branch booking and operations software for spas, salons, gyms and clinics in Nepal, built by Zunkiree Labs. See the product at <a href="https://zennly.io/" class="text-[#111827] underline hover:text-[#5a9100]" target="_blank" rel="noopener">zennly.io</a>.
  </p>
</div>

